      <p class="/_attributes/common-attributes.md"></p>
      <p>You can use the NBDE Tang Server Operator to automate the deployment of a Tang server in an OpenShift Container Platform cluster that requires Network Bound Disk Encryption (NBDE) internally, leveraging the tools that OpenShift Container Platform provides to achieve this automation.</p>
      <p>The NBDE Tang Server Operator simplifies the installation process and uses native features provided by the OpenShift Container Platform environment, such as multi-replica deployment, scaling, traffic load balancing, and so on. The Operator also provides automation of certain operations that are error-prone when you perform them manually, for example:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>server deployment and configuration</li>
      <li>key rotation</li>
      <li>hidden keys deletion</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The NBDE Tang Server Operator is implemented using the Operator SDK and allows the deployment of one or more Tang servers in OpenShift through custom resource definitions (CRDs).</p>
      <h2 id="understanding-nbde-tang-server-operator_additional-resources" class="group scroll-mt-20">Additional resources<a href="#understanding-nbde-tang-server-operator_additional-resources" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
